hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"492","Amr ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Sa'id, from al-Yasa' ibn al-Mughirah, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the narrowness of his house, and he said: Expand upward into the sky."
"493","Abdullah ibn Muhammad and Ali ibn Sahl al-Ramliyyan narrated to us, both saying: al-Walid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Ala, from Atiyyah ibn Qays, who said: The apartments of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were of palm stalks. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on one of his expeditions, and Umm Salamah was well-off, so she replaced the stalks with bricks. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this? She said: I wanted to shield myself from the gaze of people. He said: O Umm Salamah, the worst thing in which the wealth of a Muslim man is spent is building."
"494","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Abu al-Aliyah, that al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib built an upper room, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Tear it down. He said: Shall I give in charity the like of its cost in the path of Allah? He said: Tear it down; so he tore it down."
"495","Ghassan ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Qays, who said: I saw the apartments of palm stalks covered on the outside with haircloth, and I reckon the width of the apartment from the door of the room to the door of the house was about six or seven cubits, and I estimated the inner room at ten cubits, and I think its height was between eight and nine, and the like; and I stood at the door of Aishah and it faced west."
"496","Ghassan narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Hurayth ibn al-Sa'ib: I heard al-Hasan say: I used to enter the houses of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the caliphate of Uthman ibn Affan and touch their ceilings with my hand."
"497","I recited to Qutaybah ibn Sa'id: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to you, from Muhammad ibn Hilal, who said: The door of Aishah was of teak."
